["er.eventlog.import-anchor/1",{"authority":{"logical_scope":"aep","stream_identity":"01a0cae6-7e88-710c-8913-d70d29cb7b4c","tenant":"planning"},"completeness":"available_evidence_only","evidence":[],"instance":{"entity":"aep.entity","fields":{"document":{"events":[],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":0,"id":"MIG3706531bab9d5aca8d6604023d5cd6e17b9589a7dc61d03652c6be20af347610","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/eval-record-integrity","provenance":{"created_by":"system","updated_by":"system"},"revision":4,"type":"aep.story/v1","updated_at":0}},"body":"## Finding\n\nThe eval runner's raw record defaults required producer fields to absence and conditionally checks digests, so a truncated record can bypass the comparisons that bind a verdict to its specification and stream.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nConversion accumulates stable `EVAL-RECORD-*` refusals for missing, null, empty or malformed specification id, specification digest, transcript digest and expectations. Expectations are non-empty and both digests are always checked. An absent or null verdict remains `Unknown`. One focused case covers each omitted key and a mutation deleting a required-field check turns the suite red.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `crates/protocol-cli/src/eval.rs` and eval fixtures/tests — cited from the review.\n","relations":[{"derived_from":"epic:architecture-hardening"},{"serves":"vision:O3"}],"status":"implemented","summary":"Require identity, digests and expectations and always verify them.","title":"An eval record cannot omit the facts that bind its verdict"},"lifecycle_state":"implemented"}},"id":"MIG3706531bab9d5aca8d6604023d5cd6e17b9589a7dc61d03652c6be20af347610","lifecycle_state":"recorded","revision":4,"version":1},"order":"per_kind_only","subject":["aep.entity","MIG3706531bab9d5aca8d6604023d5cd6e17b9589a7dc61d03652c6be20af347610"]}]